<title>JAPAN: TIFFE euroyen ends higher due to fall in IRS rates.</title>
<headline>TIFFE euroyen ends higher due to fall in IRS rates.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>April 15 settlement  prev settlement</p>
<p> TIFFE Euroyen 3M (Z)     99.09		   99.04</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The key December three-month euroyen futures contract ended sharply higher on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Traders said large-lot buying of the December and hedge buying related to falls in medium-term interest rate swap (IRS) rates triggered the rise in euroyen futures.</p>
<p>A long-term credit bank was detected aggressively receiving fixed interest rates in the two-, three- and four-year zones, a trader for a European brokerage house said.</p>
</text>
